  "turn_number": 6,
  "player_text": "I hold the captain's look and keep my voice just as low. \"Old secrets and unsettled scores — whose? If the brass won't name them, who around this gate still will?\"",
  "visible_motivation": "The captain says the trouble past the northwest milestone is old secrets and unsettled scores that higher command wants left buried.",
  "intended_meaning": "I want a name or a person who will say whose quarrel is waiting out there.",
  "generation_attempt_1": "You hold the guard captain's steady gaze, voice lowered with the rain-slicked tension around you. The captain exhales quietly, eyes flicking briefly toward the cluster of guards and the crowded gate. \"Old secrets and unsettled scores,\" they murmur, \"belong mostly to city watch brass and those who whisper in shadow—noble intrigues tangled with unspoken debts. Around the gate, no one openly talks; the brass has sealed lips tight. If anyone here knows more, they've learned well the price of loose tongues.\" Your best lead would be to press local informants or seek someone with ties to the city watch command—perhaps the tavern runner or a more discreet contact beyond the gate crowd.\"",
